  "result": "**Verdict: `OK`** — first and only gate run (5 of 6 unused).\n\n```\nOK\n   8 witnesses, 14 names, composes nothing\n   narrowings declared by the coder: 3\n```\n\nWhat I wrote:\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_400_2a.lean`)\n- `clsV`: the one aggregate atom `ru_aggregate v \"DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle\"`.\n- `applicability`: an intersection at which the source declares a left turn for `v`, the approach carrier `v` occupies whose entrance end is that junction, and `twoDirectional` on both the carrier's way and the other way meeting there — no divider lying on the way, two carriers of opposed designated direction (dot product ≤ −`p.same_direction_cosine_tolerance`).\n- `obligation`: a universal over the carriers the subject occupies that enter that junction and over their ways, re-stating the whole selection (occupancy, kind, entrance, junction, declared intention), requiring either the leftmost lane of its own direction or — where the carrier is no recorded lane — a signed lateral offset to the centre line of its roadway within [`p.lateral_offset_resolution`, `p.centerline_adjacent_distance`].\n- Three narrowings on `ob1`: ordinal 1 written as \"no left neighbour of its direction\" (no magnitude of the file's own), the laned/unlaned gate read at the carrier, and the duty read at every such carrier rather than one.\n\n**Witnesses**: the node's seven plus `branch_4` (not applicable — the *other* intersecting highway divided), which the divider leaves of the second way need; without it mutation adequacy would have reported them unexercised.\n\nTwo judgement calls worth your eye, both argued in `task_result.md`: the obligation does not repeat the two-directionality of the ways (implied by the applicability, and every leaf of the repetition would be unexercisable), and `st.roadway` is read in `ob1`, where the node's words tie it to the centre line, rather than in `c2`.",
